cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Atlantis, please cite it using the metadata below. The authors
  contributed equally; names are listed in alphabetical order (see AUTHORS.md).
type: software
title: "Atlantis: ML-ready archive of satellite-derived flood inundation observations"
abstract: >-
  Atlantis fetches, harmonises and archives flood inundation observations from
  VIIRS (optical), MODIS (optical) and GFM (SAR) on a common 1-arcmin grid,
  accessible via a CLI, a Python API, and a Zarr/STAC archive for machine-learning
  workflows. Developed during ECMWF Code for Earth 2026.
authors:
  - given-names: Ioannis
    family-names: Kalfas
  - given-names: Stylianos
    family-names: Lagaras
repository-code: "https://github.com/opageo/atlantis"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - inundation
  - floods
  - remote sensing
  - VIIRS
  - MODIS
  - GFM
  - Sentinel-1
  - Zarr
  - STAC
  - machine learning
